      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks a lot for the question.\nWe review the patch again, and found that our engineer make a mistake in this solution.\nWe update the log and test step in https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/249709008.\n\nThe root cause is that when reconnect a BLE mouse, GATT will load cache while HOGP still need read GATT_UUID_HID_INFORMATION, GATT_UUID_HID_CONTROL_POINT, GATT_UUID_HID_REPORT_MAP etc. There is no guarantee of the sequence of read done and BTA_HH_OPEN_EVT. So it happens that after BTA_HH_OPEN_EVT, we want to read p_cb-\u003ehid_srvc.descriptor.dsc_list, it is not ready now, it seems that our solution is just a work around, it reuses the cache value.\n\nWe will abandon this CL. Thanks.",
